    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and both its tests pass along with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`, on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\nI followed the codebase's existing idiom for derived response fields (`locality`, `householdId`), touching two files:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string field to the `Owner` schema, which generates the `setContactPreference` accessor on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a small, cohesive `@AfterMapping` method `deriveContactPreference` (CC 2, ~2 changed lines) mirroring `deriveLocality`:\n   ```java\n   ownerDto.setContactPreference(email == null || email.isBlank() ? \"PHONE\" : \"EMAIL\");\n   ```\n\n**Structural impact:** I added behaviour as a new, self-contained method rather than modifying any existing method \u2014 so no existing function's `changed_lines` is affected, and the new method carries minimal cyclomatic complexity. This keeps the biggest cost lever (`WMC_other` on an edited method) out of play entirely.",
